py with literals → but transcript contains the Write content scrubbed... the FILE /tmp/scrub.py itself would still hold literals on disk! Must ensure deletion even on error: wrap script body in try/finally: finally: os.remove(__file__) (ignore errors). Yes — try/finally is important. If python itself fails to start, file remains — handle by explicit `rm -f /tmp/scrub.py` in the same Bash command after python. `rm -f` regardless — simplest belt & braces:\n   `python3 -I /tmp/scrub.py; rc=$?; rm -f /tmp/scrub.py; echo \"exit=$rc\"`. \n\n   Sandbox: writes to ~/.claude via python — may prompt for permission; that's fine, user will approve (it's their request).\n\n   Potential gotcha: `os.walk` over ~/.claude may include huge caches (e.g., ~/.claude/downloads, shell-snapshots, statsig) — fine size-wise. Also `~/.claude/projects/-workspace/memory/` — includes MEMORY.md? doesn't matter.\n\n   Also — should the roots include `/root/.claude`? whoami is presumably /home/agent. Use HOME env; fine. And check `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`? Add `os.environ.get(\"CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR\")` if set. Cheap.\n\n   Now the summary numbers I'll be able to report: file paths + counts. E.g., \"/home/agent/.claude/projects/-workspace/<uuid>.jsonl: 14 redactions\", maybe \"history.jsonl: 1\". \n\n   Also: what if scrubbing finds matches in OTHER sessions' jsonl? Only if values were mentioned there — this is the only session with them. OK.\n\n   Now — how much narration before tools? Brief: state plan in 2-3 sentences, including the no-backup rationale (deliberate, privacy), then execute. Also mention that I'll avoid repeating the figures in chat going forward so the log stays clean — actually that's implied; say it in final message instead (\"I've kept the figures out of this message so the log stays clean\").\n\n   Final message contents (clean, no literals):\n   - Done: scrubbed N occurrences of the income and debt-repayment amounts from <files>, replaced with $[INCOME]/$[DEBT] placeholders; everything